Ukraine administrative boundaries and region crosswalks (prompt 081), generated by
scripts/build-ukr-regions.py on 2026-10-13. Used by ai.foresignal.reference.ukr.UaRegionIndex to give
alerts.in.ua and siren.pp.ua alerts an oblast or raion polygon.

adm1.geojson, adm2.geojson
  Derived from geoBoundaries (https://www.geoboundaries.org), gbHumanitarian UKR ADM1 (boundary
  UKR-ADM1-82583831) and ADM2 (boundary UKR-ADM2-22097711), the "_simplified" GeoJSON of release commit
  9469f09 of https://github.com/wmgeolab/geoBoundaries. Original source: State Scientific Production
  Enterprise "Kartographia", via the Humanitarian Data Exchange (OCHA common operational dataset), year
  represented 2022. License: Creative Commons Attribution 3.0 IGO
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/igo/).
  Changes: each polygon simplified (Douglas-Peucker, at most 1,500 vertices), coordinates rounded to
  4 decimals, properties replaced by Foresignal ids and names; Kyiv city and Sevastopol given their own ids.
  Attribution: "Boundaries: geoBoundaries (Runfola et al. 2020), State Scientific Production Enterprise
  Kartographia via OCHA HDX, CC BY 3.0 IGO."
  Boundaries are administrative, as of 2022; they are not a statement about control of territory.

alerts-in-ua-uids.json
  Built from the alerts.in.ua location list linked from https://devs.alerts.in.ua/ (UID, name, type, in
  oblast/raion/hromada order), matched to the boundaries above by romanized name.

siren-region-ids.json
  Built from https://siren.pp.ua/api/v3/regions (the siren.pp.ua region tree), matched the same way.
